---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import EcosystemMap from "@/components/about/EcosystemMap.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Visitor Guide — NEXAH" description="Enter NEXAH through image, sound and a public map of its distinct responsibilities.">
  <header class="container page-hero visitor-guide-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Visitor Guide</p>
    <h1>Welcome.<br />There is no correct path.<br />Only your next step.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Enter slowly. Begin with image and sound, then use the public map to understand where you are and where you may continue.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="container visitor-prelude" aria-label="How to enter">
    <article>
      <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Enter</p><h2>Begin anywhere.</h2><p>Bring one real question. The Library does not prescribe a correct path.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Explore</p><h2>Follow curiosity.</h2><p>Let images open space. Let sound guide attention.</p></div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Connect</p><h2>Notice relationships.</h2><p>Representations may meet without collapsing their differences.</p></div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="visitor-film" aria-labelledby="film-title">
    <div class="container visitor-film__inner">
      <header class="visitor-film__header">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A visual threshold</p>
          <h2 id="film-title">Framework of Legibility</h2>
          <p class="visitor-film__subtitle">A museum of orientation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="visitor-film__invitation">
          <p>This is not a documentary.<br />It is an initiation.</p>
          <small>A journey in sound and vision · 2:48<br />Headphones recommended</small>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="visitor-film__frame">
        <video
          controls
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          poster="/media/framework-of-legibility-poster.jpg"
          aria-describedby="film-description"
        >
          <source src="/media/framework-of-legibility.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support embedded video. <a href="/media/framework-of-legibility.mp4">Open the film directly.</a>
        </video>
      </div>
      <div class="visitor-film__footer">
        <div class="visitor-film__footer-copy">
          <p id="film-description">The film moves through rooms, maps, light and shadow. It makes structure visible without prescribing where to go next.</p>
          <p class="visitor-film__credit">
            <span>Music by</span>
            <a
              class="visitor-film__credit-link"
              href="https://open.spotify.com/artist/0Fgm1un1KLYrqJRIBWKfBt?si=7u_sy9Y5S1-yQ6bplDH52Q"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Prod.Jupiter <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="visitor-film__map-link" href="#map-title">Continue to the public map <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section visitor-map-section" aria-labelledby="map-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Now see how the places relate</p><h2 id="map-title">Four places. Four responsibilities.</h2></div>
      <p>NEXAH is the Orientation Ecosystem. This canonical Version 1 map contains only public responsibilities that exist today.</p>
    </div>
    <EcosystemMap />
  </section>
  <section class="container section" aria-labelledby="paths-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Continue from the map</p><h2 id="paths-title">Choose a public place.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="boundary-grid">
      <article class="boundary-card"><strong>I want a personal beginning.</strong><p>Go to <a href="/atlas/">Start Here</a> and choose an existing work by intention or interest.</p></article>
      <article class="boundary-card"><strong>I want to understand.</strong><p>Read the publication <a href="/library/visitors-guide/">The Visitor’s Guide</a>, then try one session in NEXAHEDRON.</p></article>
      <article class="boundary-card"><strong>I want to research.</strong><p>Enter the <a href="/laboratory/">Laboratory</a> or continue to the NEXAH Research &amp; Framework Repository.</p></article>
      <article class="boundary-card"><strong>I want to inspect the core.</strong><p>Read the certified baseline in the ORION repository. ORION does not own Human meaning or decisions.</p></article>
      <article class="boundary-card"><strong>I want to experience it.</strong><p>Open <a href="https://nexahedron.com">NEXAHEDRON</a> with one real question. You may stop at Rest without invoking ORION.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section section--line" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="principles-panel">
      <blockquote id="limits-title">Version 1 makes orientation inspectable.<br />It does not make decisions.</blockquote>
      <div><p>The Human retains intention, meaning, acceptance and responsibility. NEXAHEDRON is a reference implementation. ORION is a deterministic certified core. Neither is an automatic authority.</p><a class="button" href="/about/">Understand the boundaries <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
